IRAF's own data tables, shipped with harwood so that it never needs IRAF
installed -- or available anywhere -- to run.

  linelists/   laboratory wavelengths of arc lamps (thar, henear, cuar...),
               read as linelists$thar.dat
  onedstds/    flux standards (spec50cal, spec16cal, oke1990...) and
               extinction curves (kpnoextinct.dat...), read as onedstds$...
  ccddb/       instrument header translations, read as ccddb$kpno/direct.dat
  obsdb.dat    the observatories (noao/lib/obsdb.dat), ISO-8859-1 as IRAF has it
  catalogs/    photometric standards catalogs (Landolt, Elias, UKIRT ...),
               with their format files f*.dat and equation templates
               t*.dat, read as photcal$catalogs/ by mkconfig
  mkconfig/    the help mkconfig shows at its prompts (?): catsection.key,
               obsection.key, transection.key, from photcal$mkconfig/
  scr/         the help gtools pages (:/help, and ? after w): gtools.key and
               gtwindow.key, from lib$scr/

Copied unchanged from IRAF 2.18.1 (iraf-community; the Ubuntu packages
iraf 2.18.1-2build1 and iraf-noao 2.18.1-2build1) on 2026-10-20, from
noao/lib/linelists, noao/lib/onedstds, noao/imred/ccdred/ccddb and
noao/lib/obsdb.dat; catalogs/ from noao/digiphot/photcal/catalogs on
2026-10-29, mkconfig/ from noao/digiphot/photcal/mkconfig on 2026-11-04, scr/ from lib/scr on 2026-11-04, its README from the iraf-community repository. The ccddb *.cl files are kept too: they are lists of
parameter settings (ccdproc.trim = yes), which setinstrument reads and puts
in the project file -- harwood reads them, it does not run them. The other
cl scripts (airvac.cl, mkbbcal.cl) were left out.

The tables are measurements made by others and distributed with IRAF -- the
standards are Oke's, Hayes', Massey's and the rest, as the files themselves
say. They are not edited here: a standard star's flux reproduced by hand is a
flux with a new error in it.

